belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * be-azerty-fix system keeps the earlier DECIMAL and CAPS choice when run
    again without them (saved in /var/lib/belgian-azerty-windows/choices);
    before, a rerun switched Belgian (Comma) back to Period.
  * be-azerty-fix: find the session type through logind, so that under sudo
    a Wayland session is no longer treated as X11 (setxkbmap ran against
    Xwayland).
  * postrm: take caps:be_windows out of /etc/default/keyboard when the
    package is removed, and remove the saved choices on purge.

