belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged version. The Caps Lock option, written by hand by earlier
    versions of be-azerty-fix.sh into xkb-data's files, is now owned by this
    package: the symbols file is a package file and the evdev rule is kept
    through a dpkg diversion and a file trigger, so it survives xkb-data
    upgrades however they are installed (apt or plain dpkg).
  * be-azerty-fix: new "uninstall" command; Cinnamon defaults for new users
    and reset settings (Mint); reports every failed step.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
